title: The reviewer found one bug, now fixed, and asked for more tests.
pid: ecdb6c84-e6af-463f-9482-cb757b1ec705
body: |2-
  A fresh subagent reviewed 07e3719d..f990587e against Jeff's words.
  Bug: Emacs reuses a search's buffer when the same terms are searched
  again, and the buffer kept a switch to the user's while the server
  drew the search afresh, so its mode line lied and its next save would
  be refused by the tamper check. Fixed in 5ee1e438, with a test that
  fails without the fix. Also asked for: tests that the server restores
  the old choice when a privacy challenge stops the switch, and an Emacs
  test of the retry after one. Not written; see below. Smaller
  convention fixes were made. It saw no simpler design.
